To structure your Spring Boot application in a clean and modular way, it's a good idea to separate the database operations into a dedicated service class. Here's how you can split the logic into multiple classes: one for database operations (DAO), and another for processing business logic (like generating the CorrelationId and handling FreeMarker templates).

### 1. *Create a Separate DAO Class for Database Operations*

This class will handle all database-related operations, including querying the Oracle database.

#### DatabaseService.java

java
package com.example.ftl_project.Service;

import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.jdbc.core.JdbcTemplate;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

@Service
public class DatabaseService {

    @Autowired
    private JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate;

    // Method to fetch MasterRefId from Oracle database
    public String fetchMasterRefId() {
        // SQL query to retrieve the MasterRefId (modify this as per your actual requirement)
        String sql = "SELECT SUBSTR(GWY.ERR_TXT, INSTR(GWY.ERR_TXT, 'GW') + 2) FROM YOUR_TABLE GW WHERE ROWNUM = 1";

        try {
            // Fetching the MasterRefId
            return jdbcTemplate.queryForObject(sql, String.class);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
            return null;  // Handle error, maybe log or return a default value
        }
    }
}


### 2. *Create a Service Class for Business Logic and Template Processing*

This class will generate the CorrelationId, fetch the MasterRefId from the DatabaseService, and handle FreeMarker template processing.

#### JsonTOJsonService.java

java
package com.example.ftl_project.Service;

import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import freemarker.template.Configuration;
import freemarker.template.Template;
import freemarker.template.TemplateException;

import java.io.StringWriter;
import java.io.StringReader;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.UUID;

@Service
public class JsonTOJsonService {

    @Autowired
    private DatabaseService databaseService;  // Injecting the DatabaseService

    // Method to generate a CorrelationId (UUID)
    public static String generateCorrelationId() {
        return UUID.randomUUID().toString();
    }

    // Method to process the FreeMarker template with dynamic values
    public String processTemplate(String jsonContent, String ftlContent) {
        StringWriter writer = new StringWriter();
        try {
            // Set up FreeMarker configuration
            Configuration cfg = new Configuration(Configuration.VERSION_2_3_31);
            Template template = new Template("template_xml", new StringReader(ftlContent), cfg);

            // Convert JSON content into Map using Jackson
            ObjectMapper objectMapper = new ObjectMapper();
            Map<String, Object> dataModel = objectMapper.readValue(jsonContent, Map.class);

            // Generate CorrelationId
            String correlationId = generateCorrelationId();
            // Fetch MasterRefId from database using DatabaseService
            String masterRefId = databaseService.fetchMasterRefId();

            // Add CorrelationId and MasterRefId to the data model for template processing
            dataModel.put("correlationId", correlationId);
            dataModel.put("masterReferenceId", masterRefId);

            // Process the FreeMarker template with the data model
            template.process(dataModel, writer);

        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
        return writer.toString();
    }
}


### 3. *Controller Class for Handling API Requests*

This class will handle the HTTP requests, interact with the service class, and return the appropriate response.

#### JsonToJsonController.java

java
package com.example.ftl_project.Controller;

import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.PostMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestBody;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;

import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Paths;

import com.example.ftl_project.Service.JsonTOJsonService;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/ftlCheck")
public class JsonToJsonController {

    @Autowired
    private JsonTOJsonService jjService;  // Injecting the JsonTOJsonService class

    // Endpoint to convert JSON to XML with dynamic CorrelationId and MasterRefId
    @PostMapping(value = "/JtoX", consumes = "application/json", produces = "application/json")
    public String generateXml(@RequestBody String jsonContent) {
        try {
            // Load the FreeMarker template for XML (provide correct path)
            String ftlContent = new String(Files.readAllBytes(Paths.get("src/main/resources/templates/Actual_project/toXML_create.ftl")));

            // Generate XML output with CorrelationId and MasterRefId injected into the template
            String xmlOutput = jjService.processTemplate(jsonContent, ftlContent);

            // Return the generated XML output
            return xmlOutput;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
            return "Error processing template: " + e.getMessage();
        }
    }
}


